{"id":"mahabharata-13-060","work":"mahabharata","part":13,"partName":"अनुशासनपर्व","partNameEn":"Anushasana Parva","unit":60,"title":"षष्टितमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 60 · Gift and sacrifice compared","summary":{"en":"Yudhishthira asks which of gift and sacrifice brings the greater reward in the next world, and to whom and when. Bhishma tells him to think of his own giving as sacrifice and to honour those who offer sacrifice, so that a share of their merit is his, and to protect his kin and friends as Kubera guards his riches.","kn":"ದಾನ ಮತ್ತು ಯಜ್ಞಗಳಲ್ಲಿ ಪರಲೋಕದಲ್ಲಿ ಹೆಚ್ಚು ಫಲ ಯಾವುದಕ್ಕೆ, ಯಾರಿಗೆ, ಯಾವಾಗ ಎಂದು ಯುಧಿಷ್ಠಿರ ಕೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ. ತನ್ನ ದಾನವನ್ನೇ ಯಜ್ಞವೆಂದು ಭಾವಿಸಿ ಯಜ್ಞಕಾರರನ್ನು ಗೌರವಿಸಿದರೆ ಅವರ ಪುಣ್ಯದ ಪಾಲು ಸಿಗುತ್ತದೆ, ಬಂಧು-ಮಿತ್ರರನ್ನು ಕುಬೇರ ಸಂಪತ್ತು ಕಾಯುವಂತೆ ರಕ್ಷಿಸಬೇಕೆಂದು ಭೀಷ್ಮ ಹೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"युधिष्ठिर पूछते हैं कि दान और यज्ञ में परलोक में किसका फल बड़ा है, किसे और कब। भीष्म कहते हैं कि अपने दान को ही यज्ञ मानें और यज्ञ करने वालों का सम्मान करें ताकि उनके पुण्य का अंश मिले, और बन्धुओं-मित्रों की कुबेर की तरह रक्षा करें।","te":"దానం, యజ్ఞంలో పరలోకంలో ఏది ఎక్కువ ఫలమిస్తుంది, ఎవరికి, ఎప్పుడని యుధిష్ఠిరుడు అడుగుతాడు. తన దానాన్నే యజ్ఞంగా భావించి యజ్ఞం చేసేవారిని గౌరవిస్తే వారి పుణ్యంలో వాటా దొరుకుతుందని, బంధు మిత్రులను కుబేరుడు సంపదను కాపాడినట్లు కాపాడాలని భీష్ముడు చెబుతాడు.","ta":"தானம், வேள்வி இவற்றில் மறுமையில் எது அதிகப் பலன் தரும், யாருக்கு, எப்போது என்று யுதிஷ்டிரர் கேட்க, தம் தானத்தையே வேள்வியாகக் கருதி வேள்வி செய்வோரை மதித்தால் அவர்கள் புண்ணியத்தில் பங்கு கிடைக்கும், உறவினர் நண்பரைக் குபேரன் செல்வத்தைக் காப்பது போலக் காக்க வேண்டும் என்று பீஷ்மர் கூறுகிறார்.","ml":"ദാനവും യാഗവും, ഇവയിൽ ഏതാണ് പരലോകത്ത് വലിയ ഫലം നൽകുന്നത്, ആർക്ക്, എപ്പോൾ എന്ന് യുധിഷ്ഠിരൻ ചോദിക്കുന്നു. സ്വന്തം ദാനത്തെ യാഗമായി കാണണമെന്നും, യാഗം ചെയ്യുന്നവരെ ആദരിക്കണമെന്നും, അങ്ങനെ അവരുടെ പുണ്യത്തിൽ ഒരു പങ്ക് തനിക്കും ലഭിക്കുമെന്നും ഭീഷ്മർ പറയുന്നു; കുബേരൻ തന്റെ സമ്പത്ത് കാക്കുന്നതുപോലെ ബന്ധുക്കളെയും സുഹൃത്തുക്കളെയും കാക്കണമെന്നും അദ്ദേഹം പറയുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 13.60; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Tue Nov 03 2026","sections":[{"title":"आनुशासनिकपर्व","titleEn":"Anushasanika Parva (The instructions)","verses":[{"text":"युधिष्ठिर उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Yudhishthira said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"दानं यज्ञक्रिया चेह किं स्वित्प्रेत्य महाफलम् ।\nकस्य ज्यायः फलं प्रोक्तं कीदृशेभ्यः कथं कदा ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Gift and the performance of sacrifice: which has the greater fruit after death? Which is said to have the greater fruit, to whom is it given, how, and when?"}},{"n":2,"text":"एतदिच्छामि विज्ञातुं याथातथ्येन भारत ।\nविद्वञ्जिज्ञासमानाय दानधर्मान्प्रचक्ष्व मे ॥","meaning":{"en":"I wish to know this exactly, Bharata. Wise one, explain to me, who am eager to learn, the duties of giving."}},{"n":3,"text":"अन्तर्वेद्यां च यद्दत्तं श्रद्धया चानृशंस्यतः ।\nकिं स्विन्निःश्रेयसं तात तन्मे ब्रूहि पितामह ॥","meaning":{"en":"What is the highest good among what is given within the altar with faith and compassion, dear one? Tell me that, grandfather.\""}},{"text":"भीष्म उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Bhishma said:"}},{"n":4,"text":"रौद्रं कर्म क्षत्रियस्य सततं तात वर्तते ।\nतस्य वैतानिकं कर्म दानं चैवेह पावनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"The kshatriya's work is always terrible, dear one; for him the work of sacrifice and giving here are purifying."}},{"n":5,"text":"न तु पापकृतां राज्ञां प्रतिगृह्णन्ति साधवः ।\nएतस्मात्कारणाद्यज्ञैर्यजेद्राजाप्तदक्षिणैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"But good people do not accept gifts from kings who do wrong; for this reason a king should offer sacrifices with fees properly obtained."}},{"n":6,"text":"अथ चेत्प्रतिगृह्णीयुर्दद्यादहरहर्नृपः ।\nश्रद्धामास्थाय परमां पावनं ह्येतदुत्तमम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"And if they would accept, the king should give day after day, with the highest faith; this is the best purifier."}},{"n":7,"text":"ब्राह्मणांस्तर्पयेद्द्रव्यैस्ततो यज्ञे यतव्रतः ।\nमैत्रान्साधून्वेदविदः शीलवृत्ततपोन्वितान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Let him satisfy brahmins with wealth, and then, firm in his vows, in the sacrifice, those who are friendly, good, learned in the Vedas, and endowed with character, conduct and austerity."}},{"n":8,"text":"यत्ते तेन करिष्यन्ति कृतं तेन भविष्यति ।\nयज्ञान्साधय साधुभ्यः स्वाद्वन्नान्दक्षिणावतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Whatever they do with it will be counted as done by you. Perform sacrifices for the good, with sweet food and with fees."}},{"n":9,"text":"इष्टं दत्तं च मन्येथा आत्मानं दानकर्मणा ।\nपूजयेथा यायजूकांस्तवाप्यंशो भवेद्यथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Regard yourself as having sacrificed and given through the act of giving; honour those who offer sacrifices so that you too may have a share."}},{"n":10,"text":"प्रजावतो भरेथाश्च ब्राह्मणान्बहुभारिणः ।\nप्रजावांस्तेन भवति यथा जनयिता तथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Support brahmins with many children and many dependants; he becomes a man with offspring by that, as if he were the father."}},{"n":11,"text":"यावतो वै साधुधर्मान्सन्तः संवर्तयन्त्युत ।\nसर्वे ते चापि भर्तव्या नरा ये बहुभारिणः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Whatever the good and virtuous practise as righteous duties, all those men who carry many burdens should be maintained."}},{"n":12,"text":"समृद्धः संप्रयच्छस्व ब्राह्मणेभ्यो युधिष्ठिर ।\nधेनूरनडुहोऽन्नानि च्छत्रं वासांस्युपानहौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Being prosperous, Yudhishthira, give to brahmins cows, bulls, food, umbrellas, clothes and sandals."}},{"n":13,"text":"आज्यानि यजमानेभ्यस्तथान्नाद्यानि भारत ।\nअश्ववन्ति च यानानि वेश्मानि शयनानि च ॥","meaning":{"en":"Give ghee to those who sacrifice, and food and drink, Bharata, and carriages with horses, houses and beds."}},{"n":14,"text":"एते देया व्युष्टिमन्तो लघूपायाश्च भारत ।\nअजुगुप्सांश्च विज्ञाय ब्राह्मणान्वृत्तिकर्शितान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"These gifts, Bharata, are to be given, productive of good fortune and easy to make, after you recognize brahmins unblamed and worn down in their livelihood."}},{"n":15,"text":"उपच्छन्नं प्रकाशं वा वृत्त्या तान्प्रतिपादय ।\nराजसूयाश्वमेधाभ्यां श्रेयस्तत्क्षत्रियान्प्रति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Provide for them a livelihood, whether covertly or openly; for a kshatriya this is better than the Rajasuya and Ashvamedha."}},{"n":16,"text":"एवं पापैर्विमुक्तस्त्वं पूतः स्वर्गमवाप्स्यसि ।\nस्रंसयित्वा पुनः कोशं यद्राष्ट्रं पालयिष्यसि ॥","meaning":{"en":"Thus freed from sins and purified you will reach heaven, if you protect the kingdom after again emptying your treasury."}},{"n":17,"text":"ततश्च ब्रह्मभूयस्त्वमवाप्स्यसि धनानि च ।\nआत्मनश्च परेषां च वृत्तिं संरक्ष भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"And then you will attain union with Brahma, and wealth; protect the livelihood of yourself and of others, Bharata."}},{"n":18,"text":"पुत्रवच्चापि भृत्यान्स्वान्प्रजाश्च परिपालय ।\nयोगक्षेमश्च ते नित्यं ब्राह्मणेष्वस्तु भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Care for your servants and subjects like sons, and let the security and welfare of brahmins always be your concern, Bharata."}},{"n":19,"text":"अरक्षितारं हर्तारं विलोप्तारमदायकम् ।\nतं स्म राजकलिं हन्युः प्रजाः संभूय निर्घृणम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"A king who does not protect, who takes and plunders, and who does not give: that cruel scourge of a king the people should gather together and kill."}},{"n":20,"text":"अहं वो रक्षितेत्युक्त्वा यो न रक्षति भूमिपः ।\nस संहत्य निहन्तव्यः श्वेव सोन्माद आतुरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The king who says 'I will protect you' and does not protect should be killed by all together, like a mad, diseased dog."}},{"n":21,"text":"पापं कुर्वन्ति यत्किंचित्प्रजा राज्ञा ह्यरक्षिताः ।\nचतुर्थं तस्य पापस्य राजा भारत विन्दति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Whatever wrong subjects do when unprotected by the king, a fourth of that sin the king takes, Bharata."}},{"n":22,"text":"अप्याहुः सर्वमेवेति भूयोऽर्धमिति निश्चयः ।\nचतुर्थं मतमस्माकं मनोः श्रुत्वानुशासनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Some say all of it, others say half, but our view, having heard Manu's instruction, is a fourth."}},{"n":23,"text":"शुभं वा यत्प्रकुर्वन्ति प्रजा राज्ञा सुरक्षिताः ।\nचतुर्थं तस्य पुण्यस्य राजा चाप्नोति भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"And whatever good subjects do when well protected by the king, a fourth of that merit too the king gains, Bharata."}},{"n":24,"text":"जीवन्तं त्वानुजीवन्तु प्रजाः सर्वा युधिष्ठिर ।\nपर्जन्यमिव भूतानि महाद्रुममिव द्विजाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"May all the people live on you while you live, Yudhishthira, as beings live on the rain cloud, and birds on a great tree,"}},{"n":25,"text":"कुबेरमिव रक्षांसि शतक्रतुमिवामराः ।\nज्ञातयस्त्वानुजीवन्तु सुहृदश्च परंतप ॥","meaning":{"en":"as demons on Kubera and the gods on Indra; and may your kinsmen and friends live on you, scourge of foes.\""}}]}]}